## Before reporting completion

- Validate inputs, schemas, the unit of analysis, deterministic exemplars, QC,
  machine-readable metrics, provenance, and a reproducible command when the task
  changes a scientific pipeline.
- Run the tests and pipeline targets proportionate to the change; state anything
  not run and why.
- Re-read the `README.md` contract and use `git status` plus ignore/DVC checks to
  audit every created or touched artifact.
- Confirm no accidental duplicate, cache, notebook output, or generated result
  is staged.
- Hand off human-gated actions explicitly; do not claim they occurred.

## Never do this merely to finish a task

- Edit generated files in `results/` or pipeline-owned files in `data/interim/`
  or `data/processed/` by hand.
- Turn an exploratory notebook or scratch note into a pipeline dependency.
- Introduce an unpinned dependency or weaken a quality gate.
- Commit a generated result because it is small; deliveries have their own
  immutable, provenance-carrying lifecycle.
- Rewrite Git history, force-push, delete user files, or perform broad cleanup
  without explicit authorization.
